KG42.register("clusters-9acf96b4fea8a4382130392b",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v142-d-CL003","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","label":"Ex-post SDR pricing driven by metered supply and demand and individual settlement","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL003","label":"Ex-post SDR pricing driven by metered supply and demand and individual settlement","market_meaning":"Based on historical metered supply and demand, main-grid electricity prices and compensation parameters, the ESC forms P2P buying and selling prices and uses them for the individual bills of contracted customers. The supply-demand ratio endpoints, the zero-compensation case and the benefit narrative of appropriate compensation are retained separately; mathematical gaps in bill signs and benefit comparison mean that complete settlement and benefit guarantees are still not closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation","bidding","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"The product aggregate, ex-post prices and bills have a clear information interface, and the consumer Rule-Chain provides the contract object. The battery sign in the settlement net position conflicts with the product supply-demand accounting basis, and the extension of prosumer quantities to all customers is also unclear. Pricing and billing are both ex-post activities, and no iterative dependency between pricing and real-time control is established on that basis.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This Rule-Cluster is assembled around the specific function from metered inputs to prices and then to bills, and retains the limited link from cost assessment to compensation adjustment. P2G serves only as a comparison baseline; the zero-compensation, appropriate-compensation and penetration-rate cases each have their own conditions and are not merged into an unconditional rule of benefit for all.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the supply-demand ratio, compensation management, price bounds and segmented buying and selling prices, which are the formation rules for the prices required by bills."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Take the prices and individual metered inputs to form bills, and retain the conditional benefit comparison and its mathematical doubts."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only cite the existing aggregate supply-demand definition as the input accounting basis for the supply-demand ratio; the primary attribution remains in the participation and transaction-organization Rule-Cluster, and no product rule is additionally counted."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only connect the stated consumer contracting and payment obligations to the settlement activity; the consumer participation permission is not counted again as an independent rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19"],"rationale":"Eq. (17) explicitly forms the supply-demand ratio from the aggregate supply and demand stated in the product Rule-Chain; this is an interface from the aggregate definitions to the ratio calculation, not an equivalence of two expressions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::theta_Pr_sell","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g03-E10"],"rationale":"The P2P selling price given by Eq. (19) is the price input adopted by the seller branch of Eq. (37); only the price output and settlement use are connected, and the still-questionable net-position sign is not endorsed."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C009"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::theta::theta_Pr_buy","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g03-E10"],"rationale":"The P2P buying price given by Eq. (20) is the price input adopted by the buyer branch of Eq. (37); the source clarifies its use, and the connection does not claim across categories that the expression and the parameter are the same object."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e013"],"rationale":"After consumers contract with the ESC, their payment obligation is implemented by P2P pricing and the ex-post billing activity; the participation obligation and the bill-calculation responsibility are complementary and are not collapsed as duplicate constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C009"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C004","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C013"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"Zero compensation with a supply-demand ratio greater than one is a specific case within the same segmented pricing mechanism, explaining the price consequences and revenue-risk narrative of the settlement Rule-Chain; it is not generalized to results at other compensation levels."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C014"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E13"],"rationale":"The source uses an upper bound on the buying price to support the consumer bill comparison, but a zero supply-demand ratio also allows the buying price to be equal; this connection locates the argumentative interface, the missing premise for strict benefit is recorded in G009, and no scientific implication edge is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C010","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C011"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g04-E12"],"rationale":"The source states that individual cost and participation-willingness assessment help the ESC adjust the compensation price, so bill comparison and compensation management have a functional link; the participation-willingness indicator and parameter-adjustment algorithm have not entered the current Rule-Chain, and this connection is not completed as an automatic feedback rule."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R007::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g02-E10"],"rationale":"Both places refer to the ESC in the same community responsible for compensation management and customer bills. The representative citation is for display only; the pricing and settlement responsibilities and the original objects are all retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R007::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"],"rationale":"Both places are the same P2P pricing function of that community, carrying price formation and bill use respectively. The benefit-inference edge and the bill-association edge in the settlement Rule-Chain still retain different meanings and are not deduplicated merely because the node display is merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-SDR","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_SDR"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"The community supply-demand ratio at the same time is used both to calculate prices and as the zero-compensation condition of the settlement Rule-Chain. The two local uses as calculation input and condition parameter are retained, and it is not rewritten as a single object."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_comp"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g04-E12"],"rationale":"The source uses the same compensation price managed by the ESC for price formation and for explaining revenue impact; the two local parameters and their respective unit records remain independent, and the allowable interval is not interpreted as a sufficient condition for benefit to all."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda-buy","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_buy"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g03-E07"],"rationale":"The same main-grid electricity purchase price serves respectively as the P2P buying-price reference and as a P2G bill input. Only the physical-economic meaning is associated; local roles and case units are retained, and any numerical currency conversion must be clarified separately."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda-sell","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_sell"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E07"],"rationale":"The same main-grid electricity selling price is used for the P2P selling price and compensation conditions, and also for P2G revenue accounting. The different local parameters and unit expressions are retained, and the numerical records are not directly merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-P-aggBC","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBC"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g03-E09"],"rationale":"Only within the intersection of the same defined prosumer and time do the allocated charging powers of Eq. (13) enter Eq. (17) and Eq. (36). The pricing input and settlement input remain independent; the consumer index extension and bill sign are not confirmed by this association."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-MAP008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-P-aggBD","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBD"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g03-E09"],"rationale":"Only within the intersection of the same defined prosumer and time do the allocated discharging powers of Eq. (15) enter the supply-demand ratio and the individual bill. The local uses in each Rule-Chain are retained, and this quantity is not equated with the R001 control variable for which no interface has been established."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"unverified_source","description":"All connections and identity mappings in this Rule-Cluster are formed on the basis of unaudited B evidence. Repeated citations, formal consistency among formulas or the present semantic analysis cannot raise source_status.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C009","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C011","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e006","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the source, transcription and interpretation; continue to retain unverified and candidate attributes, and do not claim completion of B audit, C2 independent review or scientific acceptance."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Eq. (3) defines net load as load minus photovoltaics, whereas in R007-C011/C012 the charging term lowers the billed net load and the discharging term raises it, which cannot be consistently closed with the supply subtraction/addition directions of R006-C002 and R005-C004.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_NP","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBC","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBD","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C011","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the original formulas, transcription and positive power direction, and then have C clarify the relationship between product supply-demand and the settlement net position; D retains the existing formulas, and does not reverse signs on its own or claim that the bill is closed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R007-C014 derives a strict bill decrease from a non-strict buying-price upper bound and a no-export condition, lacking comparability of electricity consumption and conditions that produce strict savings; R005-C006 also allows the P2P buying price to equal the main-grid buying price.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C014"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E08","v141-b-g03-E13"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify the common electricity-consumption baseline for bill comparison and the strict-improvement conditions, distinguishing non-increase from strict decrease; retain the frozen inference and do not treat the source's qualitative assertion as a proven theorem."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G010","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The supply-demand ratio does not address total demand being zero, and the price segmentation does not clarify whether negative supply-demand ratios are excluded; when the supply-demand ratio is zero and the sum of the main-grid selling price and the compensation price is zero, the C008 fraction may be undefined, and the precedence relationship between the C006 endpoint text and the fraction is also not stated.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C006","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C008","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C should clarify, based on the source, the domains of applicability of supply-demand and electricity prices, the non-zero denominator condition and the treatment of degenerate endpoints; D does not add default prices or replace frozen expressions with limits."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G011","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source definitions of net load and battery allocation quantities target prosumers, whereas individual bills are extended to all customers; the input conventions for consumers without photovoltaics or batteries are unclear. C012 lacks a zero-net-position branch, and the index convention when prices are selected by customer also needs explanation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-P-aggBC","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-P-aggBD","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_NP","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBC","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_P_aggBD","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_Pr","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C012"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g02-E01","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E10"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C should clarify the customer index range, the input definition for customers without devices, the customer dependence of prices and the treatment of zero net position; zero values must not be inserted or new branches added based on common sense."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G012","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R007-C001 states the ESC's payment-balance responsibility, but the current Rule-Chain has no identity that uniformly accounts for the aggregation of individual bills, PCC main-grid exchange and payments to external suppliers, so it cannot be concluded on that basis that complete cash receipts and payments are balanced.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C010","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C011"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g02-E27","v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E09"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C should complete the accounting boundary between internal receipts/payments and main-grid settlement, and check the total bill amount after the net-position sign is clarified; D does not substitute a responsibility description for a budget-balance proof."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G013","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The compensation-price interval and the ESC's adjustment responsibility do not provide a parameter-selection procedure that guarantees benefit for every customer. The participation-willingness indicator has not entered the current Rule-Chain, and the penetration-rate sensitivity results and the summary of appropriate compensation cannot replace general sufficient conditions, nor do they imply equal benefits.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C005","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g03-E11","v141-b-g03-E12","v141-b-g04-E08","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E11","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E17"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"C should supplement source-supported evaluation inputs and compensation-selection conditions, distinguishing case thresholds, qualitative summaries and general guarantees; the respective condition scopes of the zero-compensation and appropriate-compensation cases are maintained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G014","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The compensating-price node proposal v141-b-g04-P01-compensating-price remains pending. For now, only existing compensation parameters and pricing node references can be used; the assembly cannot be interpreted as meaning that this new node has been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_comp"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E09","v141-b-g04-E11","v141-b-g04-E12","v141-b-g04-E15"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g04-P01-compensating-price"],"required_work":"Whether to adopt this ontology proposal shall be determined separately by manual review; before a decision is made, retain the frozen parameters and existing nodes, and do not add graph objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G015","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The R005 main-grid electricity price uses the case expression pence/kWh, while R007 uses currency/kWh; association of physical quantities does not mean that the numerical scales have been unified. Billing uses time integration, whereas T is defined as the number of time slots, and the time scale from discrete metering to integration is also not specified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R007"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda-buy","v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta-lambda-sell","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_buy","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_lambda_sell","v141-c-R007::theta::theta_T","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C010","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C011"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E09","v141-b-g03-E16"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Before numerical settlement, C shall specify the unit conventions for the common currency, price multiplier, and metering duration; D keeps local parameters independent and does not presume conversion or rewrite the integral."}]},"rule_refs":["19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R005","19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R007","19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R006","19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-7f5e3dcddfa1014c","COMP-a607cc256fbfc1eb","COMP-bf4a00350a51bde7","KG31-fc19e7c39ea9de54","KG40-f19328f0aeb3d626"]});
